{"type":"message","id":"15cee7c5","parentId":"113fc4c6","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:12.380Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Blueprint, a construction document intelligence engine. Read your skill file at /home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md and the processing pipeline at /home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/references/processing-pipeline.md FIRST.\n\n## Your Task\nRun the UPDATED pipeline (with Phase 1.5 Convergence Validation) on the HHC Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition project.\n\n## What's Already Done\n- Phase 0 (Intake) is COMPLETE — PDFs split, sheets classified, specs extracted\n- All 134 drawing pages are at: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_001.png through page_134.png\n- Text extracted to: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/text/\n- Sheet classification: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/classification.json\n- Sheet index: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/sheet_index.json\n- Specs: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/specs/\n- Previous takeoff (for reference only): /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/\n\n## What You Need To Do\n\n### PATH B: Schedule Extraction (PRIORITY — this was weak last time)\nExtract EVERY schedule into structured JSON files. Use the text extraction files AND image analysis of the actual drawing pages. Key pages:\n- page_022.txt/png = A-701 (Door Schedule + Partition Types)  \n- page_025.txt/png = A-801 (Finish Schedule + Finish Legend + Furniture Plan)\n- page_021.txt/png = A-501 (RCP — ceiling types, keynotes)\n- Check ALL other pages for equipment schedules, fixture schedules, panel schedules, valve schedules, light fixture schedules\n\nSave structured JSON to /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/schedules/:\n- doors.json\n- finishes.json  \n- finish_legend.json\n- partitions.json\n- millwork.json\n- ceiling_keynotes.json\n- Any other schedules found\n\n### PATH A: Drawing Takeoff (visual count from plans)\nGo through the floor plans (especially A-101 page_008.png or nearby), RCP, elevations and VISUALLY COUNT:\n- Door swings/marks on plans\n- Room tags on plans\n- Partition type tags on plans\n- Fixture/equipment symbols\n- Any other countable items\n\nSave to /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/drawing_counts.json\n\n### PHASE 1.5: Convergence Validation\nCompare Path A vs Path B for EVERY item type. Generate:\n/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/convergence_report.json\n\nFormat per the pipeline spec:\n```json\n{\n  \"doors\": {\"path_a\": X, \"path_b\": Y, \"status\": \"MATCH|MISMATCH\", \"details\": [...], \"confidence\": \"HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW\"},\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n### Bid Sheet Mapping\nThe bid sheet has 132 line items. Map each non-LS item to the schedule data. Use the SCHEDULE quantities as primary source, cross-checked against drawing counts.\n\nUpdate /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/quantities.json with corrected quantities.\n\n### Key Corrections From Last Run\n- Item 48 (Storefronts): Should be 6 EA not 3 — count each AL door as individual unit (ED-1-02, 03, 04, 06, 07, 08)\n- ED-1-05 is missing from door schedule — flag it, investigate on plans\n- Access panels (Item 47): Drawing note says \"not quantified on drawings\" — flag appropriately\n\nBe EXTREMELY thorough on schedule extraction. Every row, every column, every field. This is the core improvement."},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1770064452378}}
{"type":"message","id":"93e8de93","parentId":"15cee7c5","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:16.880Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the skill file and pipeline, then work through this systematically.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SgV1bSftGPwjsaEAzZYQnJ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ANtbQbQR4z8m2siyyxrrWN","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/references/processing-pipeline.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AsN3Xo13dH4BLJVB33ZXmJ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/sheet_index.json"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":3,"output":223,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":12644,"totalTokens":12870,"cost":{"input":0.000015000000000000002,"output":0.005575,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.079025,"total":0.084615}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770064452379}}
{"type":"message","id":"3e661502","parentId":"93e8de93","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:16.905Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01SgV1bSftGPwjsaEAzZYQnJ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# BluePrint — Construction Document Intelligence Engine\n\n> Chat-based preconstruction intelligence engine that reads a full project set like an expert estimator.\n\n## Purpose\n\nBluePrint ingests complete construction document sets (drawings + specifications), builds a structured understanding of the entire project, and provides scope intelligence for pricing. It thinks like a builder: demo first → room-by-room → cross-reference everything → flag the gotchas → quantify.\n\n**Completeness is the mission.** Missing scope/quantities is the #1 risk. BluePrint's primary job is making sure nothing slips through.\n\n## Core Rule\n\n> **Flag, don't assume.** If it's not on the drawings, flag it — never silently include inferred scope.\n\n## Triggers\n\nActivate BluePrint when the user:\n- Uploads construction drawings (PDF sets)\n- Uploads specifications (CSI-format PDFs)\n- Asks about project scope, finishes, partitions, quantities, takeoffs\n- Requests CSI division summaries, RFQ packages, or scope reports\n- Asks construction Q&A questions about a loaded project\n- Uses keywords: blueprint, plan review, scope, takeoff, RFQ, CSI, finish schedule, partition, demo\n\n## Trade Configuration\n\nBluePrint reads the **entire project** across all CSI divisions. Trade profiles control what gets full analysis vs. coordination-only flagging.\n\n### Trade Profiles\n\n| Profile | Focus Divisions | Use Case |\n|---------|----------------|----------|\n| Interior GC (default) | Demo, Concrete/Masonry, Rough Carpentry, Finish Carpentry, Painting, Flooring/Tiling + flex (Drywall, Doors, Specialties) | Doug's default |\n| Full GC | All CSI divisions | Full general contractor |\n| MEP | Div 21-28 | Mechanical/Electrical/Plumbing |\n| Custom | User-defined | Any trade combination |\n\n### Focus vs. Coordination\n- **Focus trades**: Full scope analysis, quantities, pricing intelligence, RFQ generation\n- **Coordination-only trades**: Flag for coordination impacts (e.g., \"mechanical diffuser in ceiling — confirm ceiling grid coordination\")\n\nSwitching trade profile re-filters existing analysis — no reprocessing required.\n\n### 6 Core Trades (Default Interior GC)\n1. **Demolition** — Existing conditions removal\n2. **Concrete/Masonry** — Structural/architectural concrete and masonry\n3. **Rough Carpentry** — Framing, blocking, backing\n4. **Finish Carpentry** — Millwork, trim, casework\n5. **Painting** — All paint/coating scopes\n6. **Flooring/Tiling** — All floor and wall tile/flooring scopes\n\n### Flex Trades (Configurable per project)\n- Drywall (Div 09 21 16)\n- Doors/Frames/Hardware (Div 08)\n- Specialties (Div 10)\n- Others as needed\n\n## Processing Pipeline\n\nSee `references/processing-pipeline.md` for full detail.\n\n### Overview\n```\nPHASE 0: INTAKE\nPHASE 1: PAGE-BY-PAGE INGESTION\n  ├── PATH A: Drawing Takeoff (visual count from plans)\n  └── PATH B: Schedule Extraction (parse from schedule tables)\nPHASE 1.5: CONVERGENCE VALIDATION (Path A quantities == Path B quantities?)\nPHASE 2: ROOM-BY-ROOM SYNTHESIS\nPHASE 3: Q&A READY\n```\n\n- **Intake**: Upload PDF set → split, classify, OCR\n- **Phase 1 — Dual-Path Extraction** (runs in parallel):\n  - **Path A — Drawing Takeoff**: Count items visually from floor plans, RCPs, elevations (e.g., count doors on plans, measure wall lengths, count fixtures)\n  - **Path B — Schedule Extraction**: Parse every schedule table into structured data (door schedule, finish schedule, partition types, equipment, fixtures, panels, valves, lighting)\n- **Phase 1.5 — Convergence Validation**: Compare Path A and Path B quantities. Match = HIGH confidence. Mismatch = flag for review with both counts and sources.\n- **Phase 2**: Room-by-room synthesis — build room inventory, apply finishes/partitions/doors, categorize scope by trade, generate flags\n- **Q&A Ready**: Conversational interface active\n\nProcessing time: **Overnight is acceptable** for a 30-sheet set. Thoroughness > speed.\n\n### Schedule Extraction Rules (Phase 1, Path B)\n\n> **MANDATORY: Full extraction of ALL schedules before ANY quantity work begins.**\n\nBluePrint must identify and fully extract every schedule in the drawing set. No exceptions, no summarizing — raw table data, every row, every column.\n\n#### Required Schedule Checklist\nBefore proceeding to Phase 2, ALL of the following must be confirmed PRESENT or ABSENT:\n\n- [ ] Door Schedule (mark, room, size, type, material, frame, glazing, rating, hardware set, remarks)\n- [ ] Finish Schedule (room, floor, base, walls N/S/E/W, ceiling type, ceiling height)\n- [ ] Finish Legend (every finish code → manufacturer, product, color, dimensions, notes, rep contact)\n- [ ] Partition Type Schedule (type, construction, stud size/gauge, GWB layers, STC, fire rating, height, special requirements)\n- [ ] Hardware Schedule (set number, items, manufacturers)\n- [ ] Equipment Schedule (ID, description, location, furnished/installed by)\n- [ ] Plumbing Fixture Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Electrical Panel Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Light Fixture Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Valve Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Millwork Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Responsibility Matrix / OFI-OFCI (if present)\n\n#### Extraction Format\nEach schedule is parsed into a **structured JSON array** — not prose, not summaries. Example:\n```json\n// doors.json\n[\n  {\"mark\": \"ED-1-01\", \"room\": \"Cart Wash\", \"type\": \"D\", \"width\": \"5'-0\\\"\", \"height\": \"7'-0\\\"\", \"material\": \"HM\", \"finish\": \"TF\", \"glazing\": null, \"frame_width\": \"5'-4\\\"\", \"frame_material\": \"HM\", \"frame_glazing\": null, \"rating\": \"3\", \"hw_set\": \"1.0\", \"remarks\": \"\"}\n]\n```\n\n#### Cross-Reference Validation (Phase 1.5)\nAfter both paths complete, automatically check:\n1. Every door mark on floor plans appears in door schedule (and vice versa)\n2. Every room on floor plans appears in finish schedule (and vice versa)\n3. Every partition type tag on plans has a matching type in partition schedule\n4. Every fixture/equipment tag on plans has a matching schedule entry\n5. Quantities from Path A (visual count) match quantities from Path B (schedule count)\n6. **Flag ALL orphans** in either direction — items on plans but not in schedules, or in schedules but not on plans\n7. **Flag ALL mismatches** with both counts and sources: \"Path A counted 6 doors on A-101, Path B found 8 doors in schedule — investigate ED-1-05 (in schedule but not found on plan)\"\n\n## Data Model\n\nSee `references/data-model.md` for full schema.\n\n### Key Entities\n- **Project** → Floors → Rooms (atomic unit)\n- **Room**: Floor → Room Name → Room Number (hierarchy)\n- **Partitions**: Shared objects between rooms — two faces, each side has its own finish belonging to the room it faces\n- **Demo Items**: Separate section (not nested under rooms)\n- **Schedules**: Finish, Door, Hardware, Equipment, Responsibility Matrix\n- **Flags**: Considerations, inferences, coordination items, conflicts, orphans\n\n## Flag Types\n\nBluePrint generates 8 types of flags:\n\n| Flag Type | Description | Example |\n|-----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Inferred Scope** | Work implied but not drawn | \"Epoxy demo → heavy floor prep likely needed\" |\n| **Coordination Impact** | Other-trade work affecting focus trades | \"Mechanical diffuser — confirm ceiling grid\" |\n| **Owner-Furnished** | OFI/OFCI items to exclude from pricing | \"Owner-furnished appliances per responsibility matrix\" |\n| **Atypical Condition** | Unusual detail worth noting | \"Existing window AC removal — investigate infill\" |\n| **Conflict** | Drawing vs. spec disagreement | \"Plan shows FT-1 in Room 101, finish schedule shows FT-2\" |\n| **Orphan Reference** | Callout to nonexistent detail/sheet | \"Detail 4/A3.2 called out but sheet A3.2 not in set\" |\n| **Missing Information** | Expected data not found | \"Room 105 not on finish schedule\" |\n| **Exclusion Recommended** | Item to specifically exclude for risk mitigation | \"FT-3 in finish schedule but not found on any drawing\" |\n| **Access/Height Impact** | Scope item requires non-standard access method | \"Painting exposed structure at 21' AFF — lift/scaffold required\" |\n\n## Outputs\n\n### On-Demand Commands\n| Command | Output | Format |\n|---------|--------|--------|\n| **CSI Summary** | Scope organized by CSI Division | PDF |\n| **Room Quantities** | Per-room geometry + applied finishes with quantities | Excel |\n| **Trade Breakdown** | Scope organized by trade | PDF/Excel |\n| **RFQ Package** | Subcontractor pricing request with scope, products, spec references | PDF |\n| **Flags Report** | All flags/considerations organized by type | PDF |\n| **Q&A** | Conversational answers to scope questions | Chat |\n\n### RFQ Package Contents\n- Scope description\n- Products/materials (from specs + schedules)\n- Relevant drawing references\n- Relevant specification sections\n- Quantities toggle: **ON** (include quantities) or **OFF** (scope only, let sub price)\n\n### CSI Division Summary Format\n```\nDivision 09 - Finishes\n  09 21 16 - Gypsum Board Assemblies\n    • Partition Type A: 3-5/8\" steel stud, 5/8\" GWB ea. side\n    • Partition Type B: 6\" steel stud, (2) layers 5/8\" Type X ea. side, 2-hr rated\n    • Locations: [list]\n  09 30 00 - Tiling\n    • FT-1: Porcelain tile, 12x24, [manufacturer]\n    • Locations: Bathrooms 101, 103, 105\n    • Quantity: ~450 SF\n```\n\n## Q&A Behavior\n\nWhen answering questions:\n1. Answer directly with the requested information\n2. If multiple answers exist (e.g., multiple corridor wall types), state all of them\n3. Ask clarifying questions when needed to give an accurate answer\n4. Never guess — if the data isn't in the documents, say so and flag it\n5. Keep answers concise but complete\n\n## Specifications Handling\n\n- Format: Typically one large PDF (1,000+ pages)\n- Method: **Text extraction** (not vision) — specs are text-heavy\n- CSI divisions have standard formatting → slice intelligently\n- **Priority divisions**: 02 (Existing Conditions/Demo), 03 (Concrete), 04 (Masonry), 06 (Wood/Carpentry), 07 (Thermal/Moisture), 08 (Doors), 09 (Finishes), 10 (Specialties)\n- **Primary use**: Verify products/materials/means & methods from drawing callouts\n- Flag abnormal installation methods or substrate prep requirements\n\n## Project Management\n\n- **Multi-project**: Support 2-5 simultaneous projects\n- **Storage**: Cloud-based (Dropbox or watched folder)\n- **History**: All analyzed data persists for future pricing reference\n- **Cloud AI**: Processing through cloud vision/language APIs is acceptable\n- **Security**: Bid documents are not confidential\n\n## Quantity Takeoff Roadmap\n\n- **v1**: Scope identification + organization (what goes where, by trade)\n- **v2**: Room-based quantities from extracted geometry (perimeter LF, area SF, wall SF per room → apply finishes)\n- **v3**: Full scaled measurement from drawings (or lean on Kreo/Bluebeam integration)\n\n## UX\n\n- **Interface**: Chat-based (Telegram) — upload docs, ask questions, receive files\n- **Output delivery**: Excel and PDF files sent directly in chat\n- **Target user**: Solo estimator/preconstruction lead\n- **Device**: Desktop with large monitor (primary), laptop (mobile)\n- **Presentation**: Volume of detail, clean formatting, clear/concise\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n1. **Completeness is the mission** — missing scope is the #1 risk\n2. **Flag, don't assume** — if it's not on the drawings, don't silently include it\n3. **Read the ENTIRE project** — all CSI divisions, not just focus trades\n4. **Partitions are shared objects** — they live between rooms, each face belongs to its adjacent room\n5. **Demo is separate** — demolition items are their own section, not nested under rooms\n6. **Cross-reference everything** — trace callouts to details, schedules to specs\n7. **Detect conflicts and orphans** — if a reference points to nothing, flag it\n8. **Exclusion flagging** — if something is on a schedule but not on drawings, recommend explicit exclusion\n9. **Distinguish ceiling paint from wall paint at high-bay spaces** — When a room has an exposed structure ceiling (no ACT/GWB), the ceiling paint finish (e.g., P-1) applies to the OVERHEAD STRUCTURE (deck, joists, beams), not to the full-height walls. Always clarify: \"painting exposed overhead structure at X' AFF\" vs. \"painting partition walls at standard height.\" This distinction is a major cost driver (lift/scaffold for overhead vs. standard for walls) and must be explicitly stated in scope summaries and RFQs.\n10. **Separate access/height considerations for every scope item** — When ceiling heights exceed standard (~10'), flag the access method impact: lift, scaffold, or swing stage. Call out the specific height and what's being accessed (exposed structure, high walls, columns). This affects pricing for painting, drywall, ceiling installation, demo, and MEP coordination.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770064456904}}
{"type":"message","id":"c86c42be","parentId":"3e661502","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:16.908Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01ANtbQbQR4z8m2siyyxrrWN","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# BluePrint — Processing Pipeline\n\n## Overview\n\n```\nPHASE 0: INTAKE\nPHASE 1: DUAL-PATH EXTRACTION (parallel)\n  ├── PATH A: Drawing Takeoff (visual count from plans)\n  └── PATH B: Schedule Extraction (parse from schedule tables)\nPHASE 1.5: CONVERGENCE VALIDATION (Path A == Path B?)\nPHASE 2: ROOM-BY-ROOM SYNTHESIS\nPHASE 3: Q&A READY\n```\n\nTarget: **30-sheet set processed overnight.** Thoroughness > speed.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0: Intake\n\n**Trigger**: User uploads PDF document set (and optionally specifications PDF).\n\n### Steps\n1. **Receive documents** — Accept PDF uploads via chat\n2. **Split PDF** — If multi-page PDF, split into individual pages\n3. **Classify pages** — Determine discipline and sheet type for each page:\n   - Cover sheet\n   - Demo plans (D-series)\n   - Floor plans (A-series)\n   - Reflected ceiling plans (RCP)\n   - Elevations, sections, details\n   - Schedules (finish, door, hardware, equipment)\n   - Legends and general notes\n   - Structural (S-series) — coordination\n   - MEP (M/E/P-series) — coordination\n4. **Create project record** — Initialize project with metadata from cover sheet (name, location, owner)\n5. **Apply trade profile** — Set default Interior GC profile or user-specified profile\n6. **Queue for processing** — Order sheets logically (cover → demo → plans → RCPs → details → schedules)\n\n### Spec Intake (Parallel)\n1. **Receive spec PDF** — Typically one large PDF (1,000+ pages)\n2. **Text extraction** — Extract all text (NOT vision — specs are text documents)\n3. **Division slicing** — Parse CSI division structure, identify division boundaries\n4. **Priority indexing** — Index priority divisions first: 02, 03, 04, 06, 07, 08, 09, 10\n5. **Product extraction** — Extract product names, manufacturers, acceptable substitutes per section\n6. **Store spec sections** — Each section stored with summary, products, and installation notes\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Page-by-Page Ingestion\n\n**Goal**: Catalog everything. Extract all data. Build the raw knowledge base.\n\n### Step 1.1: Sheet Reading\nFor each sheet (in order):\n- Run vision model on full sheet image\n- Extract: title block, sheet number, scale, date, revision\n- Capture all text, callouts, keynotes, annotations\n\n### Step 1.2: Element Extraction\nFor each sheet, identify and extract:\n- Room numbers and names\n- Room boundaries (where detectable)\n- Partition type callouts and locations\n- Door marks and locations\n- Finish callouts\n- Detail callouts (e.g., \"See Detail 4/A3.2\")\n- Section callouts\n- Keynotes and general notes\n- Dimensions (where legible)\n\n### Step 1.3: Schedule Parsing\nFor schedule sheets, extract structured data:\n- **Finish schedule**: Code → description → rooms → product\n- **Door schedule**: Mark → type → size → rating → hardware set → rooms\n- **Hardware schedule**: Set → items → manufacturers\n- **Equipment schedule**: ID → description → location → furnished/installed by\n- **Responsibility matrix**: Item → furnished by → installed by\n\n### Step 1.4: Demo Plan Analysis\nFor demolition sheets:\n- Identify all demolition items\n- Categorize: wall removal, ceiling removal, floor removal, fixture removal, etc.\n- Note existing conditions being removed\n- Flag considerations (e.g., \"existing epoxy demo → heavy prep/patching\")\n- Record locations\n\n### Step 1.5: Cross-Reference Mapping\nFor all extracted callouts:\n- Map detail references to target sheets/details\n- Map finish codes to finish schedule entries\n- Map door marks to door schedule entries\n- Map partition type codes to partition type details/legends\n- Map spec section references to extracted spec content\n- **Flag orphans**: Any reference that doesn't resolve to an existing target\n\n### Step 1.6: Legend & General Notes Processing\n- Extract all partition type legends with full assembly descriptions\n- Extract all keynote legends\n- Extract general notes (may contain scope, means/methods, or standards)\n- Cross-reference abbreviations and symbols\n\n### Step 1.7: Coordination Sheet Scan\nFor structural and MEP sheets (coordination-only):\n- Light-touch scan for items impacting focus trades\n- Flag: ceiling-mounted equipment, structural penetrations, duct routing affecting ceiling grids\n- Do NOT do full scope analysis on coordination sheets\n\n### Phase 1 Output\n- All sheets cataloged with extracted content\n- All schedules parsed into structured data (Path B)\n- All drawing-based counts completed (Path A)\n- All cross-references mapped (resolved or flagged as orphans)\n- All demo items cataloged\n- Raw data ready for convergence validation\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1.5: Convergence Validation\n\n**Goal**: Compare Path A (drawing takeoff) and Path B (schedule extraction) quantities. Two independent paths that MUST converge on the same numbers. Mismatches are the most valuable findings.\n\n### Step 1.5.1: Quantity Comparison\nFor every countable item type, compare:\n\n| Item Type | Path A Source | Path B Source |\n|-----------|--------------|---------------|\n| Doors | Count door swings/marks on floor plans | Count rows in door schedule |\n| Rooms | Count room tags on floor plans | Count rows in finish schedule |\n| Partition types | Count unique type tags on plans | Count types in partition legend |\n| Fixtures | Count fixture symbols on plans | Count rows in fixture schedule |\n| Equipment | Count equipment tags on plans | Count rows in equipment schedule |\n| Light fixtures | Count symbols on RCP | Count rows in light fixture schedule |\n| Panels | Count panel symbols on electrical plans | Count rows in panel schedule |\n\n### Step 1.5.2: Classification\nFor each comparison:\n- **MATCH** → Mark as HIGH confidence, proceed\n- **MISMATCH** → Flag for review with:\n  - Path A count + source sheets\n  - Path B count + source schedule\n  - Specific items that don't reconcile (e.g., \"ED-1-05 in schedule but not on plan\")\n  - Recommended resolution\n\n### Step 1.5.3: Orphan Detection\nCross-reference in both directions:\n- **On plan but not in schedule**: Item exists on drawings but has no schedule entry → Flag as `missing_information`\n- **In schedule but not on plan**: Item has schedule entry but can't be found on drawings → Flag as `exclusion_recommended` or `missing_information`\n\n### Step 1.5.4: Convergence Report\nGenerate `convergence_report.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"doors\": {\"path_a\": 8, \"path_b\": 8, \"status\": \"MATCH\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\"},\n  \"rooms\": {\"path_a\": 5, \"path_b\": 5, \"status\": \"MATCH\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\"},\n  \"partitions\": {\"path_a\": 4, \"path_b\": 7, \"status\": \"MISMATCH\", \"note\": \"Path B includes existing types A-D not tagged on new plans\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\"},\n  \"orphans\": [\n    {\"item\": \"ED-1-05\", \"direction\": \"gap_in_sequence\", \"note\": \"Door marks skip from ED-1-04 to ED-1-06\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**HARD GATE: Phase 2 does NOT begin until convergence validation is complete.** All mismatches must be documented. Resolution is not required (some mismatches are expected), but they must be acknowledged.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Room-by-Room Synthesis\n\n**Goal**: Reorganize all extracted data by room. Apply finishes. Generate scope. Flag issues.\n\n### Step 2.1: Room Inventory\n- Build master list of all rooms from floor plans\n- Organize by Floor → Room Name → Room Number\n- Cross-reference with finish schedule to verify completeness\n- Flag any rooms on plans but not on schedule (and vice versa)\n\n### Step 2.2: Room Geometry\nFor each room:\n- Extract or calculate perimeter (linear feet)\n- Extract or calculate area (square feet)\n- Calculate wall surface area (perimeter × ceiling height)\n- Note ceiling height (from RCP, sections, or general notes)\n- Source: measured from scaled drawings (v2+) or extracted from annotations\n\n### Step 2.3: Finish Application\nFor each room:\n- Look up finish schedule entry by room number\n- Apply floor finish (code + description + product from spec)\n- Apply wall finish\n- Apply ceiling finish\n- Apply base finish\n- **Flag**: Room on schedule with finish code not found in specs\n- **Flag**: Room on plans but not on finish schedule\n\n### Step 2.4: Partition Assignment\nFor each room:\n- Identify all bounding partitions from floor plan\n- Look up partition type from legend/detail\n- Create partition objects with two faces\n- Assign room + finish to each face\n- Extract partition properties: stud size, layers, fire rating, STC rating, height, sealants\n- **Flag**: Partition type called out but not in legend\n- **Flag**: Unusual partition requirements (height to structure, special ratings)\n\n### Step 2.5: Scope Categorization\nFor each room, categorize all work by trade and CSI division:\n- Demolition scope (from demo plans)\n- New partition construction (from floor plans + partition types)\n- Ceiling work (from RCP)\n- Floor finishes (from finish schedule)\n- Wall finishes (from finish schedule)\n- Painting (from finish schedule + painting notes)\n- Doors/frames/hardware (from door schedule)\n- Millwork/casework (from elevations + details)\n- Specialties (from plans + specs)\n- Tag each item with CSI division and section\n\n### Step 2.6: Flag Generation\nRun completeness and intelligence checks:\n\n**Completeness checks:**\n- Every room has finishes assigned\n- Every finish code resolves to a product in specs\n- Every detail callout resolves to an existing detail\n- Every partition type resolves to a legend entry\n- Every door mark resolves to a door schedule entry\n- Responsibility matrix items are accounted for\n\n**Intelligence checks:**\n- Owner-furnished items identified and flagged for exclusion\n- Coordination impacts from MEP/structural flagged\n- Atypical conditions noted (unusual assemblies, special ratings)\n- Inferred scope flagged (NOT silently included)\n- Conflicts between drawings and specs flagged\n- Items on schedules but not on drawings → recommend explicit exclusion\n\n### Phase 2 Output\n- Complete room-by-room data with all finishes, partitions, doors, scope items\n- CSI division summary generated\n- All flags generated and categorized\n- Project status → **READY**\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Q&A Ready\n\n**Goal**: Project fully analyzed. System responds to queries conversationally.\n\n### Capabilities\n- Answer scope questions about any room, trade, or CSI division\n- Generate CSI division summaries on demand (PDF)\n- Generate room quantity reports (Excel)\n- Generate trade-specific breakdowns\n- Generate RFQ packages (with quantities toggle)\n- Generate flags/considerations report\n- Ask clarifying questions when queries are ambiguous\n\n### Q&A Rules\n1. Answer directly with requested information\n2. If multiple answers exist, state all of them\n3. Ask clarifying questions when needed\n4. Never guess — if data isn't in documents, say so and flag it\n5. Keep answers concise but complete\n6. Source information when helpful (sheet reference)\n\n---\n\n## Completeness Checklist\n\nBefore marking a project as READY, verify:\n\n- [ ] All sheets processed (no pages skipped)\n- [ ] All schedules fully extracted into structured JSON (door, finish, partition, hardware, equipment, fixture, panel, lighting, valve, millwork, responsibility matrix)\n- [ ] Path A drawing takeoff complete (visual counts from plans)\n- [ ] Path B schedule extraction complete (parsed from schedule tables)\n- [ ] **Convergence validation complete** — Path A vs Path B compared, all mismatches documented\n- [ ] All rooms inventoried and matched to finish schedule\n- [ ] All partition types resolved to legend entries\n- [ ] All cross-references mapped (orphans flagged)\n- [ ] All demo items cataloged\n- [ ] Spec sections indexed for priority divisions\n- [ ] All flags generated and categorized\n- [ ] CSI summary generated\n- [ ] Owner-furnished items identified\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Error | Action |\n|-------|--------|\n| Sheet illegible / low quality | Flag as `missing_information`, note which sheet, continue processing |\n| Schedule entry malformed | Extract what's possible, flag for manual review |\n| Cross-reference to missing sheet | Flag as `orphan_reference`, continue |\n| Spec section not found | Flag as `missing_information`, note the expected section |\n| Room on plan not on schedule | Flag as `missing_information` |\n| Room on schedule not on plan | Flag as `exclusion_recommended` |\n| Conflicting information (plan vs. spec) | Flag as `conflict`, present both versions |\n| Partition type not in legend | Flag as `missing_information`, extract whatever is visible |\n\n---\n\n## Processing Scripts (To Build)\n\n| Script | Purpose | Phase |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `split_pdf.py` | Split multi-page PDF into individual pages | 0 |\n| `classify_sheet.py` | Classify sheet discipline and type | 0 |\n| `extract_sheet.py` | Vision extraction of sheet content | 1 |\n| `parse_schedule.py` | Parse schedule sheets into structured data | 1 |\n| `extract_specs.py` | Text extraction and division slicing of specs | 0 |\n| `map_references.py` | Build cross-reference map, detect orphans | 1 |\n| `validate_convergence.py` | Compare Path A vs Path B quantities, generate convergence report | 1.5 |\n| `build_rooms.py` | Room inventory and geometry | 2 |\n| `apply_finishes.py` | Apply finish schedule to rooms | 2 |\n| `assign_partitions.py` | Partition creation and room assignment | 2 |\n| `categorize_scope.py` | Scope items by trade and CSI | 2 |\n| `generate_flags.py` | Run all flag checks | 2 |\n| `generate_outputs.py` | CSI summary, Excel, RFQ, flags report | 3 |\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770064456907}}
