{"type":"message","id":"98f178f9","parentId":"7828f7de","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:29.501Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01C9fH9kynMmg2q2Ha2sr2zm","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C - 1\nC - 1\nC - 1\nC - 1\nC - 1\nC - 1\nC - 1\nRF-4\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\n8.75\"\n5.5\"\n9\"\n9\"\n9\"\n5.5\"\n9\"\n9\"\n10\"\n3 1/2\"\nREFLECTED CEILING GENERAL NOTES\nCEILING SYMBOL LEGEND\nFIXTURE MOUNTING MATRIX\nCEILING FINISHED LEGEND\n10' - 0\"\nC-1\n10' - 0\"\nC-2\nCART WASH\n1\nSECURITY\n2\nNYPD\nSECURITY\nPICKUP\n3\nNEW ILLUMINATED SIGNAGE ABOVE\n10' - 0\"\nC-2\n9' - 0\"\n3' - 6\"\n3' - 6\"\nEQ\n10' - 0\"\n4' - 0\"\n4' - 0\"\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nLT-A\n?\n9' - 6\"\nC-2\nCART\nALCOVE\n5\nENTRANCE\nVESTIBULE\n4\n10' - 0\"\nC-2\n10' - 0\"\nC-2\nEQ\nEQ\nUNDERSIDE OF CANOPY ROOF EXISTING \nCEILING & LIGHTING TO REMAIN\nLT-A\nLT-A\nLT-E\nLT-E\nLT-E\nAP\n360\n360\nACCESS POINT\n360 CAMERA\n360 CAMERA\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nEXISTING \nSKYLIGHT \nABOVE\nA\nLT-C\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\n9' - 6\"\n5' - 0\"\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nLT-D\nC1\nC1\nC1\nC1\nC1\n3' - 2 3/4\"\n9' - 6\"\n3\"\nLT-A\nLT-A\nLT-B\nLT-B\nLT-A\nLT-A\nLT-A\n6' - 9\" +/-\n5' - 7\"\n5' - 7\"\n5' - 7\"\nC2\nC3\nC3\n10\"\n10\"\n1' - 6\"\n1' - 6\"\n2' - 0\"\n2' - 0\"\n9\"\nC8\nC7\nC8\nC8\nC5\nC8\nCL\nCL\nCL\nCL\nCL\nCL\n3\"\n3\"\nEQ\nEQ\n3\"\n4' - 9\"\n4' - 9\"\nCL\nEQ\nEQ\n2' - 10 1/2\"\n2' - 10 1/2\"\n2' - 10 1/4\"\nC6\nC6\nC4\nCL\n9\"\nC6\nC6\n5' - 0 1/2\"\n4' - 0 1/2\"\n1' - 6\"\nC10\n14' - 2\"\n1' - 0 1/2\"\nC6\nA3\nA-701\n3.B\n4.B\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nA.B\nB.B\nC.B\nE.B\nI.B\nG.B\nH.B\n6.B\nD.B\nF.B\n2.B1\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\n3 1/2\"\n8.75\"\n5.5\"\nCRICKET 1/4\" PER FT. \nSLOPE (TYP)\n9\"\n9\"\n9\"\n5.5\"\n9\"\n9\"\n10\"\nRF-4\nA8\nA-303\nA8\nA-303\nA6\nA-303\nA4\nA-303\nD5\nA-303\nD2\nA-303\nD8\nA-303\nA40\nA40\nA41\nA41\nA70\nA73\nA74\nA75\nA76\nA\nA\nBES-20\nDENOTES GWB SOFFIT/CEILING\n2x2 LIGHT FIXTURE\nCURTAIN TRACK\nWALL SCONCE\nDIRECT/ INDIRECT LIGHT \nFIXTURE\nEQ. A\nEQ. A\nEQ. B\nEQ. B\nCONTINUOUS LED TUBE AND \nBALLAST CONCEALED INDIRECT \nFIXTURE\nEXIT SIGN (SHADED AREA \nINDICATES DIRECTION OF EGRESS)\nLINEAR RETURN/SUPPLY DIFFUSER\nRETURN GRILL\nLIGHT - STEM MOUNTED\nRECESSED LED WALL WASHER\nPENDANT MOUNTED LIGHT\nDOWN LIGHT FIXTURE\nRADIANT PANEL\nUNDER CABINET TASK LIGHT\nNOTE: \nCEILING CONTRACTOR TO MEASURE EACH CEILING AREA AND ESTABLISH \nA CEILING LAYOUT TO BALANCE BORDER WIDTHS AT OPPOSITE EDGES OF \nEACH ROOM. AVOID USE OF TILES LESS THAN 6\".\nRECESSED COVE LIGHT\nSD S\nLT\nSD\nS\nLT\nTYPICAL DOUBLE DEVICE MOUNTING\nTYPICAL SINGLE DEVICE MOUNTING\nLT : LIGHT FIXTURE\nS : SPEAKER\nSD : SMOKE DETECTOR\nEQ EQ EQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nEQ\nCEILING TYPE AND FINISH \nDESIGNATION\n1. \nTHE \"LIMITS OF CONSTRUCTION\" LINES SHOWN ON THE ARCHITECT'S \nREFLECTED CEILING PLANS APPLY ONLY TO THE LIMITS OF THE \nARCHITECTURAL NEW CONSTRUCTION AND RENOVATION. SEE OTHER \nDISCIPLINES' DRAWINGS FOR THE LIMITS OF NEW CONSTRUCTION \nAND RENOVATION PERTAINING TO EACH DISCIPLINE.\n2. \nALL CEILING HEIGHTS ARE MINIMUM 8'-0\" UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE. \n3. \nALL GWB SOFFIT HEIGHTS TO BE 8'-0\" UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n4. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE COORDINATION DRAWINGS FOR \nTHE ARCHITECTS REVIEW AS REQUIRED BY THE SPECIFICATIONS THAT \nDEMONSTRATE THE COORDINATION OF ALL CEILING LOCATED \nDEVICES REQUIRED BY EACH DISCIPLINE AND TRADE.\n5. \nALL CEILING HEIGHTS MUST MEET CODE MINIMUMS FOR VARYING \nSPACE TYPES, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL NOTIFY THE ARCHITECT \nIMMEDIATELY OF ANY FIELD DISCREPANCY WHERE THE INDICATED \nCEILING HEIGHT CAN NOT BE MAINTAINED. \n6. \nFOR THE INSTALLATION OF OWNER-FURNISHED CEILING-MOUNTED \nEQUIPMENT, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL REFER BOTH TO THE OWNER-\nFURNISHED MANUFACTURER’S INSTRUCTIONS AND TO THE \nSTRUCTURAL DRAWINGS, FOR SUPPORT/INSTALLATION DETAILS.\n7. \nSPRINKLER HEADS ARE NOT INDICATED ON THE REFLECTED CEILING \nPLANS. SPRINKLER HEADS TO ALIGN WITH EACH OTHER IN BOTH \nNORTH/SOUTH AND EAST/WEST DIRECTIONS WHERE THEY OCCUR IN \nA SINGLE SPACE. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL INSTALL REQUIRED \nSPRINKLER HEADS IN ALL SPACES TO PROVIDE (100%) COVERAGE AS \nDEFINED IN NFPA. REFER TO FIRE PROTECTION DRAWINGS FOR \nLOCATIONS OF THE SPRINKLER HEADS.\n8. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL INSTALL ALL CEILING DEVICES TO ALIGN \nWITH EACH OTHER IN BOTH NORTH/SOUTH AND EAST/WEST \nDIRECTIONS AS PRACTICAL WHERE THEY OCCUR IN A SINGLE SPACE.\n9. \nNEITHER SPRINKLER HEADS NOR CONCEALED SPRINKLER HEAD \nCOVERS SHALL BE PAINTED. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL INSPECT ALL \nINSTALLED SPRINKLER HEADS AND REMOVE ANY SPRINKLER HEADS \nACCIDENTALLY PAINTED DURING CONSTRUCTION AND REPLACED \nWITH NEW SPRINKLER HEADS.\nCEILING HEIGHT DESIGNATION\nSECURITY CEILING. INSTALLATION PER SPECIFICATION REQUIREMENTS. \nALL PATIENT ACCESS AREAS MOST USE CORRECTIONAL GRADE SECURE \nCEILING, UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. \nSECURITY LIGHT FIXTURES. ALL PATIENT ACCESS AREAS MUST USE \nCORRECTIONAL GRADE SECURE CEILING, UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. \nINSTALLATION PER SPECIFICATION REQUIREMENTS.\n2' x 2' CEILING TILE NON-CORRECTIONAL \nGRADE CEILING\nGWB NON-CORRECTIONAL GRADE \nCEILING\nC-2\nC-1\nACCESS PANEL\nSPRINKLER\nSMOKE DETECTOR\nOCCUPANCY SENSOR\nRECESSED DOWNLIGHT SQUARE\n10. ACCESS PANELS ARE NOT QUANTIFIED OR INDICATED ON THE \nREFLECTED CEILING PLAN.  AS THE COORDINATION OF THE TRADES \nFOR ALL ABOVE CEILING UTILITIES WILL BE COORDINATED BY THE \nCONTRACTOR AND DEMONSTRATED THROUGH THE COORDINATION \nDRAWING SUBMITTAL REQUIREMENTS PROVIDED WITHIN THE \nSPECIFICATIONS FOR THE ARCHITECT'S REVIEW.  \n11. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WITH ALL TRADES AND \nINCLUDE ACCESS PANELS OF APPROPRIATE SIZE AND TYPE IN ALL NON \nACCESSIBLE CEILINGS AND SOFFITS WHERE ACCESS FOR UTILITIES AND \nBUILDING SERVICES ARE REQUIRED. REFER TO THE SPECIFICATIONS \nFOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION.  \n12. WHERE SUPPORT WIRES FOR ACOUSTICAL CEILING GRID CANNOT BE \nINSTALLED VERTICALLY, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE A \nUNISTRUT BENEATH THE OBSTRUCTION AS TO PERMIT WIRES TO BE \nVERTICALLY ATTACHED TO THE UNISTRUT.\n13. COORDINATE WITH OWNER SECURITY.\n14. ALL CEILINGS TO UTILIZE BLACK IRON HANGING DETAILS PER NYC \nCODE REQUIREMENTS.\n15. EXIT SIGN REQUIREMENTS:\na. \nEXITS SIGNS SHALL BE READILY VISIBLE FROM ANY DIRECTION OF \nTRAVEL.\nb. PROVIDE EXIT SIGNS TO CLEARLY INDICATE THE DIRECTION OF \nEGRESS TRAVEL IN CASES WHERE THE EXIT OR THE PATH OF \nEGRESS TRAVEL IS NOT IMMEDIATELY VISIBLE TO THE OCCUPANTS.\nc. \nINTERVENING MEANS OF EGRESS DOORS WITHIN EXITS SHALL BE \nMARKED BY EXIT SIGNS.\nd. EXIT SIGN PLACEMENT SHALL BE SUCH THAT NO POINT IN AN EXIT \nACCESS CORRIDOR OR EXIT PASSAGEWAY IS MORE THAN 100' OR \nTHE \"LISTED VIEWING DISTANCE\" FOR THE SIGN, WHICHEVER IS \nLESS, FROM THE NEAREST VISIBLE EXIT SIGN.\ne. \nEXIT SIGNS SHALL BE CENTERED OVER DOORS AND CORRIDOR.\n16. EXIT SIGNS SHOULD BE MOUNTED CLOSE TO THE WALL OVER STAIR \nDOORS.\n17. LIGHT FIXTURE QUANTITIES TO BE CONFIRMED BY THE CONTRACTOR \nBEFORE PRICING AND ORDERING\n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2025 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/25/2025 10:53:48 AM\nAutodesk Docs://6829 - H+H Bellevue Ambulance Bay Addition/6829-ARCH- ED ADDITION-25.rvt\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25 A-501 .00\nREFLECTED CEILING\nPLAN AND ROOF\nPLAN\nED AMBULANCE\nBAY ADDITION\nH+H Bellevue\n6829\n09/25/25\n462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\nISSUED SOLTUION FOR BID 2025\n1/4\" = 1'-0\"\nA3\nLEVEL 1 - ENLARGED RCP\n1/4\" = 1'-0\"\nA8\nEMERGENCY ENTRANCE CANOPY ROOF PLAN\nCEILING KEYNOTES_ED ADDITION\nC1\nNEW CAMERA\nC2\nCONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE METAL DOOR ACCESS PANEL PER SPEC AS REQUIRED FOR ACCESS TO MEP UNITS\nREQUIRING SERVICE, CONTRACTOR TO COORDINATE WITH MEP FOR REQUIRED LOCATION\nC3\nCONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE GYP BD ACCESS PANEL PER SPEC AS REQUIRED FOR ACCESS TO MEP UNITS\nREQUIRING SERVICE, CONTRACTOR TO COORDINATE WITH MEP FOR REQUIRED LOCATIONS\nC4\nAIR CURTAIN, SEE MEP DRAWINGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nC5\nLINEAR RETURN GRILLE MOUNTED ON VERTICAL FACE OF SKYLIGHT FASCIA, SEE MEP DRAWINGS FOR\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nC6\nACCESS PANEL FOR ABOVE CEILING MEP EQUIPMENT, TO BE ALIGNED WITH LIGHT OR OTHER CEILING DEVICES\nWHERE POSSIBLE. COORDINATE IN FIELD WITH ARCHITECT FOR EXACT LOCATION OF ACCESS PANEL\nC7\nLOCATED ABOVE CEILING MEP EQUIPMENT IN THIS AREA TO ALLOW ACCESS FROM ADJACENT ACCESSIBLE\nCEILING\nC8\nCONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE UNISTRUT SPANNING THE EXISTING SKYLIGHT (SECURED TO ADJACENT STRUCTURE\nAND HORIZONTALLY/DIAGONALLY BRACED AS REQUIRED FOR RIDGIDITY) ABOVE LIGHTS, CEILING SUPPORTS, OR\nANY OTHER CEILING DEVICE REQUIRING HANGING SUPPORT IN CEILING AREAS BELOW THE EXISTING SKYLIGHT\nC10\nCABINET UNIT HEATER, SEE MEP DRAWINGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nARCHITECTURAL  KEYNOTES_ED ADDITION\nA40\nEXISTING ROOF DRAIN AND OVERFLOW DRAIN REINSTALLED IN NEW ROOF, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nA41\nCONT. EXPANSION JOINT AT PERIMETER OF EXIST. BUILDING\nA70\nROOFTOP EXHAUST FAN, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nA73\nOAF UNIT, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nA74\nPROVIDE CRICKETS @ ROOFTOP UNITS AS REQ'D FOR DRAINAGE\nA75\nACCU UNIT, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nA76\nAREA OF NEW ROOFING (ROOFING TYPE 1, SEE DETAIL 5/A-303) , CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE NEW R-33 (5.5\" MIN THICKNESS)  & NEW ROOF\nMEMBRANE SLOPED TO ROOF DRAIN\nNO. DESCRIPTION\nDATE\n1\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770064469500}}
