{"type":"message","id":"839e54e7","parentId":"9e76488d","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:29.514Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01V33WHPEbceFubXPh5x1ofx","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"DOOR LEGEND\nFRAME ELEVATIONS LEGEND\nDOOR HARDWARE ABBREVIATION LEGEND\nDOOR HARDWARE NOTES\nDOOR LOCATION DIAGRAM\nEXISTING PARTITION TYPE LEGEND\nPARTITION TYPES GENERAL NOTES\nFIRE/SMOKE PARTITION GENERAL NOTES\nFRAME FINISH:\nTF\nTRANSPARENT FINISH\nOF\nOPAQUE FINISH\nMGP\nMETAL GALVANIZED PAINTED\nMP\nMETAL, PAINTED\nAL\nANODIZED ALUMINUM\nBAL\nBALLISTIC GLAZING\nUL RATING:\n20 M ; 45 M ; 1 H ; 1.5 H ; 2 H ; 3 H\nDOOR SIZE:\nSEE SCHEDULE FOR WIDTH, HEIGHT AND THICKNESS\nDOOR MATERIAL:\nSCV\nSOLID CORE W/ WOOD VENEER FACES\nSCH\nSOLID CORE W/ HARDBOARD FACES\nSCP\nSOLID CORE PLASTIC LAMINATE FACES\nSCA\nSOLID CORE ACROVYN FACES\nHM\nHOLLOW METAL\nGHM\nGALVANIZED HOLLOW METAL\nAL\nALUMINUM & GLASS\nDHM\nDETENTION HOLLOW METAL\nBAL\nBALLISTIC GLAZING\nDOOR FINISH:\nTF\nTRANSPARENT FINISH\nOF\nOPAQUE FINISH\nMGP\nMETAL GALVANIZED PAINTED\nMP\nMETAL PAINTED\nAL\nANODIZED ALUMINUM\nPL\nPLASTIC LAMINATE\nNUMBER:\nSEE FLOOR PLAN FOR DOOR NUMBER\nDOOR ELEVATION:\nSEE TYPES BELOW\nFRAME ELEVATION:\nSEE HOLLOW METAL ELEVATION LEGEND\nFRAME MATERIAL:\nWD\nWOOD\nHM\nHOLLOW METAL\nGHM\nGALVANIZED HOLLOW METAL\nAL\nALUMINUM\nDHM\nDETENTION HOLLOW METAL\nALL HM FRAMES TO BE WELDED\n2. \nLABEL IN THIS POSITION \nINDICATES PUSH-SIDE.\nAO\nAUTOMATIC OPERATOR\nCR\nCARD READER\nCK\nCIPHER LOCK\nCL\nCLASSROOM LOCK\nCO\nCLOSER\nDS\nDOOR POSITION SWITCH\nDR\nDORMITORY LOCK\nEX\nEXIT LOCK\nIL\nINSTITUTION LOCK\nIV\nINTERLOCK VESTIBULE\nMH\nMAGNETIC HOLD OPEN\nML\nMAGNETIC LOCK\nMS\nMOTION SENSOR\nOL\nOFFICE LOCK\nPL\nPASSAGE LOCK\nPV\nPRIVACY LOCK\nPD\nPRESENCE DETECTOR\nST\nSTOREROOM LOCK\n1\n2\n1. \nLABEL IN THIS POSITION \nINDICATES PULL-SIDE.\n1. \nALL HARDWARE SHALL BE 626 SATIN CHROME FINISH UNLESS NOTED \nOTHERWISE.\n2. \nALL HARDWARE IN RATED DOORS SHALL MEET THE REQUIREMENTS OF \nNFPA 80.\n3. \nCONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR SUPPLYING AND INSTALLING \nALL BUILDING SYSTEM KEYED LOCKS PER OWNER'S KEYING SYSTEM.\n4. \nMOUNTING HEIGHT OF DOOR HANDLES, PULLS, LATCHES, LOCKS AND \nOTHER OPERATING DEVICES SHALL BE INSTALLED AT 34 INCHES \nMINIMUM AND 48 INCHES  MAXIMUM ABOVE THE FINISHED FLOOR IN \nACCORDANCE WITH THE ADA STANDARDS FOR ACCESSIBLE DESIGN.\n5. \nMOUNTING HEIGHT FOR DOOR THRESHOLD SHALL NOT EXCEED 1/2 INCH \nIN HEIGHT. RAISED THRESHOLD AND FLOOR LEVEL CHANGES GREATER \nTHAN 1/4 INCH AT DOORWAYS SHALL BE BEVELED WITH A SLOPE NOT \nGREATER THAN ONE UNIT VERTICAL IN TWO UNITS HORIZONTAL (50-\nPERCENT SLOPE) IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE ADA STANDARDS FOR \nACCESSIBLE DESIGN.\n6. \nOPERABLE PARTS SHALL BE OPERABLE WITH ONE HAND AND SHALL NOT \nREQUIRE TIGHT GRASPING, PINCHING, OR TWISTING OF THE WRIST. THE \nFORCE REQUIRED TO ACTIVATE OPERABLE PARTS SHALL BE 5 POUNDS \n(22.2 N) MAXIMUM.\n7. \nDOORS SEPARATING CONDITIONED AND NON-CONDITIONED SPACES \nSHALL BE WEATHER STRIPPED OR GASKETS TO EFFECTIVELY AND RELIABLY \nLIMIT AIR INFILTRATION.\n8. \nALL PIN-TYPE HINGES ACCESSIBLE FROM THE EXTERIOR SHALL HAVE \nNON-REMOVABLE HINGE PINS. HINGES SHALL HAVE MIN. 1/4\"Ø STEEL \nJAMB STUD WITH 1/4\" MIN PROTECTION. STRIKE PLATE SHALL BE \nSECURED TO JAMBS WITH MIN 2.5\" LENGTH SCREWS.\n9. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY THAT DOOR CLOSERS AND OTHER \nHARDWARE ON A DOOR WITH 180 CLEAR SWING HINGE WILL ALLOW \nDOOR TO SWING OPEN 180 DEGREES WHEN A “180 DEGREE SWING” IS \nEITHER SHOWN ON THE FLOOR PLAN AND, OR INDICATED IN THE DOOR \nSCHEDULE\n6\"\nMIN.\n1'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-6\"\nMIN.\n4'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-6\"\nMIN.\n4'-0\"\nPULL SIDE\n> 8\"\nMIN.\n5'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-6\"\n> 8\"\nMIN.\n4'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-0\"\n6\"\nMIN.\n5'-0\"\n< 8\"\n6\"\n6\"\nMIN.\n5'-0\"\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\nNOTES:\nCLEARANCE = AREA IN WHICH THERE ARE NO \nPHYSICAL ELEMENTS CAUSING OBSTRUCTIONS.\n1'-0\" MIN. ON PUSH SIDE, WHEN DOOR HAS \nBOTH CLOSER AND LATCH.\nTHE CLEARANCES NOTED ABOVE ONLY APPLY TO \nFRONT APPROACH \nMIN.\n1'-0\"\nMIN.\n4'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-6\"\nCLEARANCE\nMIN.\n5'-0\"\nMIN.\n4'-0\"\nMIN.\n1'-6\"\nMIN.\n5'-0\"\nCLEARANCE\n6\"\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\nCLEARANCE\n#\nFRAME DETAIL IDENTIFIER\nREFER TO HOLLOW METAL FRAME DETAILS\nTYPE 3\nDOOR SCHEDULE\nSEE\nSEE DOOR SCHEDULE\n#\n#\nTYPE J (SLIDING DOOR)\nSEE SCHEDULE\nTYPE M\nTYPE MM\nSEE SCHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nTYPE N\nTYPE NN\nSEE SCHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nTYPE D\nTYPE F\nTYPE FF\nSEE SHEDULE\nSEE SHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nSCHED\nSEE\n1'-2\"\n6\"\nVARIES\n6\"\nSEE SHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nSEE SCHEDULE\nTYPE A\nTYPE AA\n3' - 0\"\nEXISTING PARTITION TO REMAIN TWO HOUR FIRE RATED SMOKE BARRIER.\nCONTRACTOR TO INSPECT AND SURVEY EXISTING CONDITION OF \nPARTITION AND PERFORM ALL NECESSARY WORK REQUIRED TO ACHIEVE \nTHE FIRE RATING FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE ABOVE. CONTRACTOR TO \nUSE MATERIALS IDENTICAL TO EXISTING MATERIALS OR MATERIALS WHOSE \nINSTALLED PERFORMANCE WILL EQUAL OR SURPASS THAT OF EXISTING \nMATERIALS.\nEXISTING PARTITION TO REMAIN WITH TWO HOUR FIRE RATING. \nCONTRACTOR TO INSPECT AND SURVEY EXISTING CONDITION OF \nPARTITION AND PERFORM ALL NECESSARY WORK REQUIRED TO \nACHIEVE THE FIRE RATING FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE ABOVE. \nCONTRACTOR TO USE MATERIALS IDENTICAL TO EXISTING MATERIALS \nOR MATERIALS WHOSE INSTALLED PERFORMANCE WILL EQUAL OR \nSURPASS THAT OF EXISTING MATERIALS.\nEXISTING PARTITION TO REMAIN ONE HOUR FIRE RATING SMOKE BARRIER.\nCONTRACTOR TO INSPECT AND SURVEY EXISTING CONDITION OF \nPARTITION AND PERFORM ALL NECESSARY WORK REQUIRED TO ACHIEVE \nTHE FIRE RATING FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE ABOVE. CONTRACTOR TO \nUSE MATERIALS IDENTICAL TO EXISTING MATERIALS OR MATERIALS WHOSE \nINSTALLED PERFORMANCE WILL EQUAL OR SURPASS THAT OF EXISTING \nMATERIALS.\nEXISTING PARTITION TO REMAIN WITH ONE HOUR FIRE RATING. \nCONTRACTOR TO INSPECT AND SURVEY EXISTING CONDITION OF PARTITION \nAND PERFORM ALL NECESSARY WORK REQUIRED TO ACHIEVE THE FIRE \nRATING FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE ABOVE. CONTRACTOR TO USE \nMATERIALS IDENTICAL TO EXISTING MATERIALS OR MATERIALS WHOSE \nINSTALLED PERFORMANCE WILL EQUAL OR SURPASS THAT OF EXISTING \nMATERIALS.\nTYPE A\nEXIST. 1 HOUR FIRE RATED PARTITION\nTYPE B\nEXIST. 1 HOUR SMOKE BARRIER\nTYPE C\nEXIST. 2 HOUR FIRE RATED PARTITION\n1. \nINSTALLATION OF METAL STUD PARTITIONS SHALL COMPLY WITH \nASTM C754.\n2. \nFOR STUD GAUGE AND THICKNESS REFER TO NON-STRUCTURAL METAL \nFRAMING DETAILS SHEET.\n3. \nEXTEND ALL STUDS TO UNDERSIDE OF STRUCTURE ABOVE. PROVIDE \nDEFLECTION TRACK AT TOP OR ANOTHER APPROVED METHOD TO \nALLOW FOR A 1\" DEFLECTION OF THE STRUCTURE.\n4. \nGYPSUM BOARD INSTALLATION SHALL COMPLY ASTM C840.\n5. \nSEE “GYPSUM BOARD SCHEDULE” FOR WALLBOARD TYPE AND \nLOCATION.\n6. \nNOTIFY ARCHITECT OF WORK TO BE PERFORMED ON EXISTING \nPARTITIONS AND PROVIDE PRICING ACCORDING TO UNIT PRICES \nOUTLINED IN SPECIFICATION SECTION 012200 “UNIT PRICES”.\n7. \nWHEN INFILLING OR ABUTTING EXISTING PARTITIONS CONTRACTOR \nTO ADD AN ADDITIONAL LAYER OF GYPSUM WALLBOARD TO \nPARTITION TYPE AND/OR SKIM COAT WALL AS REQUIRED TO PROVIDE \nA FLUSH SURFACE. THICKNESS OF GYPSUM WALLBOARD AND/OR STUD \nSIZE TO BE DETERMINED IN FIELD TO PROVIDE FLUSH SURFACE.\n8. \nTHE SOUND TRANSMISSION CLASS (STC) VALUE NOTED ON THE \nDRAWINGS IS THE LABORATORY TESTED RESULT OF THE PUBLISHED \nTEST NUMBER ACCOMPANYING THE STC VALUE. IF NO TEST NUMBER IS \nLISTED, THE STC VALUE IS A CALCULATION OF SIMILAR ASSEMBLIES \nAND THEIR LABORATORY MEDIAN STC RATINGS. ALL INSTALLATION \nDETAILS AND MATERIALS ARE TO COMPLY WITH THE UNITED STATES \nGYPSUM (USG) APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS TO MAXIMIZE INSTALLED \nACOUSTICAL PERFORMANCE. STC VALUES ARE BASED ON PARTITIONS \nCONSTRUCTED OF 20 GAUGE (30 ML) METAL STUDS 16\" O.C. FOR \nPARTITIONS CONSTRUCTED OF 18 GAUGE STRUCTURAL METAL STUDS, \nTHE STC VALUE WILL BE TWO POINTS LESS THAN THAT INDICATED IN \nTHE DRAWINGS.\n1.1 ALL FIRE RATED PARTITIONS AND SMOKE BARRIERS MUST BE INSTALLED \nPER THEIR UL DESIGN NUMBERS AND THE FOLLOWING NOTES.\n2.1 SMOKE PARTITION:\nA. SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED TO LIMIT THE TRANSFER OF SMOKE \nFROM ONE SIDE BY EXTENDING THE GYPSUM WALLBOARD \nFROM FLOOR TO UNDERSIDE OF FLOOR OR ROOF DECK ABOVE\nB. SMOKE PARTITION SHALL BE SEALED TIGHT TO FLOOR SLAB AND \nTO UNDERSIDE OF FLOOR OR ROOF DECK ABOVE, METAL DECK \nFLUTES SHALL BE FILLED WITH AN APPROVED MATERIAL TO \nLIMIT THE PASSAGE OF SMOKE AND ANY PENETRATIONS TO \nACCOMMODATE ELECTRICAL, MECHANICAL, PLUMBING, AND \nCOMMUNICATIONS SYSTEMS THAT PASS THROUGH SHALL BE \nPROTECTED AND/OR SEALED BY A SYSTEM OR MATERIAL THAT IS \nDESIGNED TO LIMIT THE TRANSFER OF SMOKE.\n3.1 SMOKE BARRIER: \nA. SHALL HAVE A MINIMUM 1 HOUR FIRE-RESISTANCE RATING.\nB. SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED TO LIMIT THE TRANSFER OF SMOKE ON \nBOTH SIDES AND SHALL EXTEND FROM FLOOR TO UNDERSIDE \nOF FLOOR OR ROOF DECK ABOVE\nC. SHALL BE SEALED TIGHT TO FLOOR SLAB AND TO UNDERSIDE OF \nFLOOR OR ROOF DECK ABOVE, METAL DECK FLUTES SHALL BE \nFILLED WITH AN APPROVED MATERIAL TO LIMIT THE PASSAGE \nOF SMOKE AND ANY PENETRATIONS TO ACCOMMODATE \nELECTRICAL, MECHANICAL, PLUMBING, AND COMMUNICATIONS \nSYSTEMS THAT PASS THROUGH SHALL BE PROTECTED AND/OR \nSEALED BY A SYSTEM OR MATERIAL THAT IS DESIGNED TO LIMIT \nTHE TRANSFER OF SMOKE.\n4.1 TOPS OF GYPSUM PARTITIONS ASSEMBLIES: \nA. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED ASSEMBLIES: CUT GYPSUM BOARD TO \nFOLLOW PROFILE OF STRUCTURAL DECK WITHIN 1\" AND APPLY \nFIRE-RESISTIVE JOINT SYSTEM PER SPECIFICATION SECTION\n078443 “JOINT FIRESTOPPING”. AT ALL RATED WALLS/BARRIERS, \nPROVIDE AN APPROVED UL TESTED \"FIRE-RESISTIVE JOINT \nSYSTEM\" TO COMPLY WITH NOTE #6.1 BELOW.\nB. SMOKE PARTITIONS: PROVIDE SMOKE SEALANT AT ALL \nINSTALLED GYPSUM BOARD/S.\nC. ACOUSTICALLY-RATED ASSEMBLIES: PROVIDE ACOUSTICAL \nSEALANT AT ALL INSTALLED GYPSUM BOARD/S PER \nSPECIFICATION SECTION 092900.\nD. TEMPORARY PARTITIONS: PROVIDE SMOKE SEALANT AT ALL \nINSTALLED GYPSUM BOARD/S AND PLYWOOD.\n5.1 BOTTOMS OF ASSEMBLIES:\nA. MINIMUM 1/4\" GAP TO MAXIMUM 1/2\" GAP AT FLOOR SLAB.\nB. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED ASSEMBLIES: COMPLY WITH INDICATED \nUL DESIGN. WHERE GAP EXCEEDS 1/2\", PROVIDE FIRE-RESISTIVE \nJOINT SYSTEM PER SPECIFICATION SECTION 078443 “JOINT \nFIRESTOPPING”.\nC. SMOKE PARTITIONS: PROVIDE SMOKE SEALANT AT ALL \nINSTALLED GYPSUM BOARD/S.\nD. ACOUSTICALLY-RATED ASSEMBLIES: PROVIDE ACOUSTICAL \nSEALANT AT ALL INSTALLED GYPSUM BOARD/S PER \nSPECIFICATION SECTION 092900. \n6.1 FOR ALL FIRE RATED WALLS/BARRIERS: \nPROVIDE APPROVED UL TESTED \"FIRE-RESISTIVE JOINT SYSTEM\" OR \n\"THROUGH-PENETRATION FIRESTOP SYSTEM\" TO COMPLY WITH ALL \nREQUIREMENTS OF EACH SPECIFIC CONDITION AS APPROPRIATE FOR ALL \nADJACENT COMPONENTS PER THE REQUIREMENTS OF THE MOST \nCURRENT EDITION \"UL FIRE RESISTANCE DIRECTORY - VOLUME 2A\", AND \nCOMPLY WITH SPECIFICATION SECTION 078413 \"PENETRATION \nFIRESTOPPING\" AND SPECIFICATION SECTION 078443 “JOINT \nFIRESTOPPING”.\n7.1. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL STENCIL PAINTED SIGNS IN RED LETTERS ON \nBOTH SIDES OF ALL FIRE WALLS, ALL RATED FIRE BARRIERS, ALL RATED \nSMOKE BARRIERS, AND ALL FIRE RATED PARTITIONS.  LOCATE BOTTOM \nOF SIGNS NO MORE THAN 12 INCHES ABOVE REMOVABLE CEILINGS, PER \nTHE REQUIREMENTS OF SPECIFICATION SECTION 099123 - INTERIOR \nPAINTING”.\nCONTRACTOR TO MODIFY EXISTING PARTITION FROM CEILING TO DECK TO \nCONFORM WITH PARTITION TYPE UL#465. CONTRACTOR, ALSO, TO INSPECT \nAND SURVEY EXISTING CONDITION OF PARTITION AND PERFORM ALL \nWORK TO MAINTAIN REQUIRED FIRE RATING FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE \nABOVE. CONTRACTOR TO USE MATERIALS IDENTICAL TO EXISTING \nMATERIALS OR MATERIALS WHOSE INSTALLED PERFORMANCE WILL EQUAL \nOR SURPASS THAT OF PARTITION TYPE UL#465 MATERIALS.\nTYPE D\nEXIST PARTITION MODIFIED TO BE 1 HOUR RATED\nTYPE 2\nMIN\n0' - 6\"\nTYPE 2A\nSAME AS TYPE 2 EXCEPT EXTEND GWB TO DECK/SLAB ABOVE\nTYPE 2B\nSAME AS TYPE 2A EXCEPT SMOKE PARTITION\nSEALANT (SEE NOTE #4.1)\nUNFINISHED FLOOR SLAB\n3 5/8\" METAL RUNNER\n5/8\" TYPE X GYPSUM WALLBOARD\n3 5/8\" METAL STUDS @ 16\" O.C. MAX.\nFINISHED CEILING\nSEALANT (SEE NOTE #5.1)\nSTC 34 (NGC 2013012)\nSTC 34 (NGC 2013012)\nEXTEND WALLBOARD 6\" MIN. \nABOVE FINISHED CEILING\nMETAL RUNNER INSTALLED \nBETWEEN STUDS\nSOUND ATTENUATION BLANKET\n(SEE NOTE #6)\nCONTINUOUS 3\" DEEP LEG \nDEFLECTION TRACK ATTACHED \nTO DECK/SLAB AT 12\" O.C. MAX.\nEXTEND WALLBOARD TO DECK/SLAB \nABOVE AT TYPE 2A AND 2B\nEXISTING WALL / COLUNM \nTYPE 7D\nTYPE 7E\n5/8\" TYPE X GYPSUM WALLBOARD\nFINISHED CEILING\nSEALANT (SEE NOTE #4.1)\nUNFINISHED FLOOR SLAB\nSEALANT (SEE NOTE #5.1)\nSTC 40\nSTC 40\nSOUND ATTENUATION BLANKET\n(SEE NOTE #6)\nCONTINUOUS 3\" DEEP LEG \nDEFLECTION TRACK ATTACHED \nTO DECK/SLAB AT 12\" O.C. MAX.\n4\"\nSTEP GYP BACK TO STUD \nABOVE BALLISTIC PANEL\nBALLISTIC RESISTANT PANEL (PER SPEC) CONTINUOUS \nFROM FLOOR TO 4\" ABOVE CEILING, PROVIDE BATTEN \nBEHIND SEAMS PER MANUFACTURE REQUIREMENTS, \nPANEL TO BE ON VESTIBULE/PUBLIC SIDE OF WALL\n4\" METAL RUNNER\n4\" METAL STUDS @ 16\" O.C. MAX.\nSAME AS TYPE 7D BUT WITH 3 5/8\" STUDS\nTYPE 7F\nSTC 40\nSAME AS TYPE 7D BUT WITH 4\" CFMF STUDS\nTYPE 7G\nSTC 40\nSAME AS TYPE 7D BUT WITH 6\" STUDS\nMAIN \"T\" BEAM\nCORNER BEAD\n5/8\" GYP BOARD CEILING\nTHREADED HANG ROD\nLIGHT FIXTURE, AS SCHEDULED, MOUNT LIGHT AS \nTIGHT TO FRAMING AS POSSIBLE\n2 1/2\" METAL STUDS @ 16\" O.C. MAX\n5/8\" GYPSUM WALLBOARD\n2 1/2\" METAL RUNNER\n\"BLACK IRON\" \nCHANNEL CLIP & \nDIRECT HANG CLIP\nLIGHT THREATED ROD OR HANG WIRE, PER \nMANUFACTURER, SECURED TO STRUCTURE ABOVE\nMAIN \"T\" BEAM\n5/8\" GYP BOARD CEILING\nTHREADED HANG ROD\n\"BLACK IRON\" \nCHANNEL CLIP & \nDIRECT HANG CLIP\nFLUSH CEILING TRANSITION ACT TO DRYWALL, \nPROVIDE ARMSTRONG FRAMEALL 7904, TAPE \nAND MUD TRANSITION INTO GYP BD GLG\nA\nFINISHED CEILING\n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2025 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/25/2025 10:53:54 AM\nAutodesk Docs://6829 - H+H Bellevue Ambulance Bay Addition/6829-ARCH- ED ADDITION-25.rvt\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25 A-701 .00\nPARTITION TYPES,\nLEGENDS, AND\nDOOR SCHEDULE\nED AMBULANCE\nBAY ADDITION\nH+H Bellevue\n6829\n09/25/25\n462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\nISSUED SOLTUION FOR BID 2025\nDOOR SCHEDULE - ED ADDITION\nDOOR\nROOM NAME\nDOOR\nFRAME\nRATING\nHARDWARE\nSET\nREMARKS\nNUMB\nTYPE\nSIZE\nMATERIAL\nFINISH\nGLAZING\n TYPE\nWIDTH\nMATERIAL\nFRAME GLAZING\nWIDTH\nHEIGHT\nED-1-01\nCART WASH\nD\n5' - 0\"\n7' - 0\"\nHM\nTF\n-\n3\n5' - 4\"\nHM\n-\n1.0\nED-1-02\nENTRANCE VESTIBULE\nM\n3' - 6 1/2\"\n7' - 8\"\nAL\nAL\nBAL\n-\n3' - 6\"\nAL\nBAL\nBALLISTIC LEVEL 3 DOOR FRAME AND\nGLAZING\nED-1-03\nNYPD SECURITY PICKUP\nM\n3' - 0\"\n7' - 8\"\nAL\nAL\nBAL\n-\n3' - 6\"\nAL\nBAL\n5.0\nBALLISTIC LEVEL 3 DOOR FRAME AND\nGLAZING\nED-1-04\nNYPD SECURITY PICKUP\nM\n3' - 0\"\n7' - 8\"\nAL\nAL\nBAL\n-\n3' - 6\"\nAL\nBAL\n6.0\nBALLISTIC LEVEL 3 DOOR FRAME AND\nGLAZING\nED-1-06\nENTRANCE VESTIBULE\nJ\n14' - 4\"\n8' - 0\"\nAL\nAL\nBAL\n-\n12' - 2 1/4\"\nAL\nBAL\n3.0\nBALLISTIC LEVEL 3 DOOR FRAME AND\nGLAZING\nED-1-07\nENTRANCE VESTIBULE\nJ\n14' - 4\"\n8' - 0\"\nAL\nAL\nBAL\n-\n12' - 2 1/4\"\nAL\nBAL\n3.0\nBALLISTIC LEVEL 3 DOOR FRAME AND\nGLAZING\nED-1-