{"type":"message","id":"37366f73","parentId":"fc2447f4","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:34:59.616Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01N16XSuJNFhgYUmuXWWkFpT","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C - 1\nDEMOLITION LEGEND\nCONTRACTOR RESPONSIBILITIES WITH\nREGARD TO EXISTING CONDITIONS NOTES\nDEMOLITION GENERAL NOTES\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nC.B\nE.B\nI.B\nG.B\n6.B\n2.B1\nDECONTAMINATION\nDECONTAMINATION\nEXISTING \nRECREATION \nDECK ABOVE \nTO REMAIN\n9'-9 1/2\"\n2'-5 1/2\"\n37'-4 1/2\"\n5'-0\"\nFHC\nDN\n35' - 4\" ±\nAPPROXIMATE SCOPE OF \nREMOVAL OF ASPHALT, \nSEE CIVIL DWGS\n39' - 9 1/4\"\n34' - 10\"\n6' - 7\"\n2' - 10 3/4\"\n47' - 0 1/2\"\n41' - 5\" ±\nD1\nD2\nD3\nD4\nD5\nD6\nD7\nD6\nD7\nD18\nD19\nA\nA\n2' - 2 3/4\"\n8' - 6\"\n3.B\n4.B\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nC.B\nE.B\nI.B\nJ.B\nK.B\n6.B\nD10\nD10\nD10\nD10\nD11\nD12\nD13\nD14\nD14\nD14\nD14\nD35\nD35\nD35\nD10\n3.B\n4.B\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nA.B\nB.B\nC.B\nE.B\nI.B\nG.B\nH.B\n6.B\nD.B\nF.B\n2.B1\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\nOD\nRD\n3 1/2\"\n8.75\"\n5.5\"\n9\"\n9\"\n9\"\n5.5\"\n9\"\n9\"\n10\"\nA8\nA-303\nD15\nD15\nD16\nD17\nD20\nD20\nD20\nD16\nD21\nE\nF\nG\nH\nJ\nB\nC\nD\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nC.B\nE.B\nI.B\nG.B\n6.B\n2.B1\nA\nDECONTAMINATION\nDECONTAMINATION\n2' - 7 3/4\"4' - 2\"\nD9\nD8\nD8\nD21\n1. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL PERFORM A SITE VISIT. IN DOING SO THE \nCONTRACTOR HAS AGREED THAT ONE HAS INVESTIGATED THE \nEXISTING CONDITIONS TO BE RENOVATED AND COMPARE THEM TO \nTHE WORK TO BE PERFORMED ACCORDING TO THE CONTRACT \nDOCUMENTS.\n2. \nTHE EXISTING INFORMATION INCLUDED WITHIN THE CONTRACT \nDOCUMENTS ARE BASED UPON INFORMATION PROVIDED BY THE \nOWNER AND FURTHER SUPPLEMENTED BY LIMITED FIELD \nOBSERVATIONS AND MEASUREMENT AND MAY NOT REFLECT ALL \nEXISTING CONDITIONS. NO GUARANTEE IS MADE AS TO THE \nGENERAL CONDITIONS OF THE EXISTING BUILDING. THE \nCONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR COMPLETE VERIFICATION OF ALL \nEXISTING FIELD CONDITIONS.\n3. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL FIELD-VERIFY THE EXISTING CONDITIONS \nAS THEY RELATED TO SPECIFIC PORTIONS OF THE WORK. \nVERIFICATION SHALL BE UNDERTAKEN IN ADVANCE TO ALLOW FOR \nTIMELY IDENTIFICATION OF EXISTING CONDITIONS THAT MAY AFFECT \nTHE SCHEDULED INSTALLATION OF NEW WORK AS DOCUMENTED \nAND TO AVOID UNDUE AND UNREASONABLE DELAYS TO THE \nPROJECT CONSTRUCTION SCHEDULE. SHOULD SUCH CONDITIONS BE \nDISCOVERED, A MINIMUM PERIOD OF TEN (10) WORKING DAYS \nSHALL BE ALLOWED FOR THE ARCHITECT TO EVALUATE THE \nCONDITIONS AND MAKE RECOMMENDATIONS TO \nACCOMMODATING WORK BASED ON ACTUAL CONDITION.\n4. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL FIELD-VERIFY THE LOCATION AND EXTENT \nOF THE LIFE SAFETY SYSTEM (INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO \nSPRINKLER SYSTEMS, SMOKE DETECTION SYSTEMS, EMERGENCY \nLIGHTING SYSTEMS) AS THEY MAY BE AFFECTED BY THE WORK. THE \nCONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR ACCOMMODATING THESE \nSYSTEMS WHEN AFFECTED BY DEMOLITION WORK SO THAT ALL \nAPPLICABLE CODES REQUIREMENTS ARE SATISFIED.\n5. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL IDENTIFY EXISTING COMPONENTS AND \nASSEMBLIES WITHIN THE BUILDING THAT ARE CONSTRUCTED AS \nFIRE-RATED ASSEMBLIES; SHALL NOTE ANY DISCREPANCIES AND/OR \nCONFLICTS INVOLVING EXISTING CONDITIONS AND BRING THEM TO \nTHE ARCHITECT'S ATTENTION IMMEDIATELY.\n6. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WITH THE OWNER ANY \nCONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES WHICH MAY IMPEDE NORMAL \nOPERATION, INCLUDING ANY ACTIVITY WHICH CREATES EXCESSIVE \nNOISE, AND NOTIFY ANY OCCUPANTS OF THE BUILDING OF ANY \nCONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES WHICH MAY AFFECT THEIR ABILITY TO \nOPERATE NORMALLY.\n7. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL TAKE ALL NECESSARY PRECAUTIONS TO \nPREVENT DAMAGE TO AREAS ADJACENT TO CONSTRUCTION OR \nOCCUPIED AREAS WHERE VARIOUS SYSTEM CONNECTIONS OR \nEXTENSIONS ARE REQUIRED AND SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR \nDAMAGE CAUSED BY CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES.\n8. \nTHE CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE BUILDING IN A WEATHER TIGHT \nCONDITION AT ALL TIMES\n9. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL IDENTIFY POINTS OF ACCESS TO THE \nBUILDING AND VERIFY MINIMUM CLEARANCES AVAILABLE FOR USE \nIN TRANSPORTING NECESSARY CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY, \nEQUIPMENT, MATERIALS, AND COMPONENTS INTO THE BUILDING.  \nUSE OF SUCH POINTS OF ACCESS SHALL BE APPROVED BY THE \nOWNER.\nREMOVE EXISTING WALL CONSTRUCTION, SHOWN WITH DASHED LINES, IN \nITS ENTIRETY FROM FLOOR TO STRUCTURE ABOVE INCLUDING DOORS, DOOR \nFRAMES, BORROWED LIGHTS, ASSOCIATED ELEC. / MECH. WORK, ETC. \nPREPARE AREA FOR NEW CONSTRUCTION.\nREMOVE EXISTING DOOR OR BORROWED LIGHT INCLUDING FRAME \nASSEMBLY, SHOWN WITH DASHED LINES.  CLOSE  EXISTING OPENING WITH \nMETAL STUDS AT 16\" O.C. AND GYPSUM BOARD ON EACH SIDE.  ALIGN NEW \nWORK FLUSH WITH EXISTING ADJACENT PARTITION. MATCH EXISTING WALL \nTHICKNESS, UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE IN ARCHITECTURAL PLAN.\nPROVIDE OPENING IN EXISTING PARTITION, SHOWN WITH DASHED LINES,  \nAS REQUIRED TO ACCOMMODATE NEW CONSTRUCTION.\nREMOVE EXISTING PLUMBING FIXTURES, SHOWN WITH DASHED LINES. \nEXISTING PIPING  SHALL BE CAPPED AS INDICATED ON THE PLUMBING \nDRAWINGS.  ANY FLOOR PENETRATIONS DUE TO THE REMOVAL OF PIPING \nARE TO BE FILLED AS NOTED IN THE CUTTING AND PATCHING GENERAL \nNOTES.\nLIMIT OF ARCHITECTURAL DEMOLITION\n1. \nALL DEMOLITION WORK EXECUTED AND MATERIAL REMOVED DURING \nDEMOLITION OPERATIONS SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE WITH THE CITY \nOF NEW YORK REQUIREMENTS AND ALL CODES AND ORDINANCES AS \nSET FORTH BY ALL AUTHORITIES HAVING JURISDICTION.\n2. \nTHE “LIMITS OF ARCHITECTURAL DEMOLITION” LINES SHOWN ON THE \nARCHITECT’S DEMOLITION PLANS APPLY ONLY TO THE LIMITS OF THE \nARCHITECTURAL DEMOLITION.  SEE OTHER DISCIPLINES’ DRAWINGS \nFOR THE LIMIT OF THEIR DEMOLITION WORK.\n3. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL BRACE ALL EXISTING STRUCTURES AND \nSTRUCTURAL ELEMENTS AS NECESSARY DURING DEMOLITION.  THE \nCONTRACTOR SHALL ENGAGE A STRUCTURAL ENGINEER TO \nDETERMINE REQUIREMENTS.\n4. \nNO FLOOR OR STRUCTURAL MEMBERS SHALL BE CUT WITHOUT \nPERMISSION OF A REGISTERED STRUCTURAL ENGINEER.\n5. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL NOTIFY THE ARCHITECT IMMEDIATELY IF ANY \nDEMOLITION WORK CANNOT BE PERFORMED DUE TO EXISTING FIELD \nCONDITIONS.\n6. \nREMOVE ALL REMNANTS OF EXISTING FLOOR FINISHED DOWN TO THE \nCONCRETE SLAB OR TOPPING SLAB, AND LEAVE FLOOR SMOOTH FOR \nNEW FINISH.  \n7. \nAFTER DEMOLITION WORK IS COMPLETE, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL \nREPAIR ALL HOLES IN EXISTING-TO-REMAIN FLOORS, WALLS, AND FIRE \nBARRIERS TO COMPLY WITH ORIGINAL FIRE/SMOKE/SOUND \nASSEMBLIES, FIRE PROTECTION REQUIREMENTS, AND STRUCTURAL \nINTEGRITY.\n8. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE THE SHUTTING DOWN OF \nACTIVE UTILITY PRIOR TO BEGINNING DEMOLITION EFFORTS.\n9. \nALL FLOOR PLANS ARE NOT TO BE SCALED. ALL FLOOR AREAS ARE \nAPPROXIMATE.\n10. THE CONTRACTOR TO REMOVE ALL MAJOR FIXED EQUIPMENT, \nMEDICAL EQUIPMENT AND ANY OTHER EQUIPMENT INCLUDING \nMISCELLANEOUS SUPPORTS, TRACKS, BUILT-IN ITEMS, MOUNTING \nBRACKETS, HARDWARE, ANCHORING DEVICES, ETC IN THEIR ENTIRETY. \nDO NOT LEAVE PORTIONS IN EXISTING CONSTRUCTION.\n11. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL REMOVE ALL ITEMS TO BE DEMOLISHED IN \nTHEIR ENTIRETY INCLUDING ALL ASSOCIATED PIPING, WIRING, \nHANGERS, SUPPORTS, PROJECTIONS, BOLTS, NAILS, ETC. FROM \nEXISTING SURFACES UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n12. REMOVE, STORE, AND PROTECT WEATHERING STEEL FOR REUSE IN \nCONSTRUCTION. FOR REMOVAL OF WEATHERING STEEL CLADDING, \nMAINTAIN FULL PANEL WIDTH AND CUT WITH STRAIGHT LINES TO THE \nGREATEST EXTENT POSSIBLE FOR PIECES TO BE REMOVED\n13. COORDINATE WITH STEEL FABRICATOR AND THEIR ENGINEER TO \nREMOVE WEATHERING STEEL ONLY TO THE EXTENT NECESSARY TO DO \nCONSTRUCTION\n14. EXISTING SPRINKLER AND PIPING TO REMAIN DURING THE EARLY \nDEMO WORK .HOWEVER, AFTER REMOVAL OF WALLS IF THE EXISTING \nSPRINKLER HEADS ARE PLACED AT A DISTANCE WHICH IS NOT IN \nCOMPLIANCE WITH NFPA-13 2016, CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE NEW \nSPRINKLER HEAD IN BETWEEN THE EXISTING HEADS AND CONNECT IT \nTO EXISTING PIPING.\n15. UPON REMOVAL OF THE WALLS, IN CASE WHERE THE EXISTING \nSPRINKLER HEADS ARE PLACED LESS THAN 6'-0\" APART, CONTRACTOR \nTO PROVIDE A BARRIER BETWEEN SUCH HEADS.\nREMOVE ALL EXISTING  CEILING TYPES, FRAMING, GRIDS LIGHTING, SUPPLY \n& RETURN DIFFUSERS, CEILING MOUNTED FIXTURES AND EQUIPMENT IN \nTHEIR ENTIRETY. UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED.\nD11\nD13\nD9\nAREA HATCHED ON PLAN SHALL REMAIN EXISTING WITH NO DEMOLITION \nSCOPE INCLUDED. ANY DAMAGE TO EXISTING PARTITIONS OR OTHER \nELEMENTS WITHIN HATCHED AREA SHOULD BE REPAIRED TO MATCH \nEXISTING CONDITION PER THE CUTTING AND PATCHING GENERAL NOTES. \nWHERE APPLICABLE, FIRE RATINGS SHOULD BE MAINTAINED.\n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2025 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/25/2025 10:54:22 AM\nAutodesk Docs://6829 - H+H Bellevue Ambulance Bay Addition/6829-ARCH- ED ADDITION-25.rvt\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25 AD-101 .00\nDEMOLITION PLANS\nED AMBULANCE\nBAY ADDITION\nH+H Bellevue\n6829\n09/25/25\n462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\nISSUED SOLTUION FOR BID 2025\n1/8\" = 1'-0\"\nA4\nDEMILITION PLAN\n1/8\" = 1'-0\"\nA7\nREFLECTED CEILING DEMOLITION PLAN\n1/8\" = 1'-0\"\nD7\nEMERGENCY ENTRANCE CANOPY ROOF PLAN\nDEMOLITION  KEYNOTES_ED ADDITIOIN\nD1\nEXISTING LIGHTED \"EMERGENCY\" SIGNAGE TO BE REMOVED, SEE MEP DRAWINGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nD2\nEXISTING STOREFRONT AND DOOR TO BE REMOVED\nD3\nDEMOLISH EXISTING CONCRETE SLAB, DIAGONAL FILLED REGION REPRESENTS APPROX SCOPE OF REMOVAL, CONTRACTOR TO COORDINATE\nEXACT SCOPE OF REMOVAL WITH NEW WORK\nD4\nDEMOLISH EXISTING SIAMESE CONNECTION, SEE MEP DRAWING\nD5\nDEMOLISH EXISTING HOSE BIBB, SEE MEP DRAWING\nD6\nREMOVE EXISTING BOLLARDS\nD7\nEXISTING BOLLARDS TO REMAIN\nD8\nCROSS HATCH REPRESENTS APPROXIMATE ROUTE OF MEP INFRASTRUCTURE INSTALLATION, REMOVE CEILING AS REQUIRED TO ACCESS\nABOVE CEILING PLENUM FOR MEP WORK. REPLACE/REPAIR CEILING AS REQUIRED AFTER COMPLETION TO MATCH EXISTING CONDITIONS. SEE\nMEP DWGS AND VERIFY IN FIELD THE SCOPE OF WORK REQUIRED.\nD9\nAPPROXIMATE LOCATION OF PULL BOX FOR ELECTRICAL CONDUIT RUN, CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE ACCESS PANEL IN CEILING WHERE\nNON-ACCESSIBLE CEILINGS EXIST. SEE MEP DWGS AND VERIFY IN FIELD THE SCOPE OF WORK REQUIRED. WHERE ACCESS PANELS ARE\nREQUIRED, CONFIRM THE EXACT LOCATION WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO INSTALLATION.\nD10\nEXISTING LIGHT TO BE REMOVED, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO.\nD11\nEXISTING LIGHT TO BE REMOVED, SEE MEP DWGS FOR ADDITIONAL INFO. CONTRACTOR TO PATCH AND REPAIR EXISTING SOFFIT @ SKYLIGHT\nAFTER REMOVAL OF EXISTING LIGHTS.\nD12\nEXISTING LIGHTS TO BE REMOVED\nD13\nEXISTING SECURITY CAMERA TO BE REMOVED AND RETURNED TO OWNER\nD14\nEXISTING EXISTING METAL PANEL CEILING TO BE REMOVED WITHIN AREA OF NEW BUILDOUT\nD15\nROOF DRAIN TO BE REMOVED & SAVED FOR REINSTALL IN NEW ROOF, SEE ROOF CONSTRUCTION PLAN FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nD16\nCONTRACTOR TO CUT EXISTING ROOF MEMBRANE @ THIS LOCATION FOR TIE-IN TO NEW ROOF MEMBRANE AS PART OF RE-ROOFING, SEE\nROOF CONSTRUCTION DRAWING FOR ADDITIONAL INFO\nD17\nCONT. EXPANSION JOINT AT PERIMETER OF EXIST. BULDG TO BE REMOVED AT LOCATION OF ROOF REMOVAL\nD18\nDEMOLISH EXISTING CURB\nD19\nREMOVE IRON FENCE AND CURB\nD20\nEXISTING SKYLIGHT TO REMAIN\nD21\nAREA OF WORK\nD35\nCONTRACTOR TO INFILL LIGHT REMOVAL WITH METAL PANEL SOFFIT PANEL TO MATCH EXIST\n3/64\" = 1'-0\"\nD4\nDEMILITION PLAN FOR CONDUIT REINSTALL\nARCHITECTURAL  KEYNOTES_ED ADDITION\nNO. DESCRIPTION\nDATE\n1\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770064499613}}
